01:01:03,157 --> 01:01:09,157
Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time is a 2010 action fantasy film based on the
video game series Prince of Persia created by Jordan Mechner.

11
01:07:09,473 --> 01:07:15,473
It was directed by Mike Newell from a screenplay by Boaz Yakin, Doug
Miro, and Carlo Bernard, based on a story by Mechner.

12
01:13:15,789 --> 01:13:21,789
The film stars Jake Gyllenhaal, Ben Kingsley, Gemma Arterton, and Alfred Molina.

13
01:19:22,105 --> 01:19:28,105
It is an adaptation of the 2003 video game of the
same name published by Ubisoft.

14
01:25:28,421 --> 01:25:34,421
Elements from its sequels Warrior Within (2004) and The
Two Thrones (2005) are also incorporated.

15
01:31:34,736 --> 01:31:40,736
Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time premiered in London on May 9, 2010, and was released theatrically in the
United Kingdom on May 21 and the United States on May 28 by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures.

16
01:37:41,052 --> 01:37:47,052
The film received mixed reviews from critics and had grossed over $336.4 million on a production budget of $150–200
million, and was the highest-grossing video game film adaptation until it was surpassed by Warcraft in 2016.

17
01:43:47,368 --> 01:43:53,368
The film explores themes of persia, sandstorm, brother
against brother, armageddon, based on video game.

